Borrowers are your students, teachers and staff. Nothing is copied: the library adds only its own
state (a block, personal limits, a count of loans) the first time someone borrows.

Open **Library → Borrowers**, search, and select a person.

## The borrower page

- **Library card**: the card number on file.
- **Loans**, **Holds**, **Fines** and **Returned** history.
- **Blocked because**: the reason they cannot borrow now. This is worked out when you look, never
  stored: loan limit, an overdue book, unpaid fines above your limit, or a block placed by hand.
- **Reserve a book** on their behalf.

## Block, unblock and personal limits

With **Add staff borrowers, block, unblock & set limits** you can block someone with a reason. They
keep the books they have; the desk refuses new loans.

Under **Own limits** set **Books at a time (0–50)** or **Loan length in days** for one person. Leave a
box empty to use the **Loan rule** for their type.

## Add a staff borrower

Non-teaching staff are not in your student or teacher lists. Use **New staff borrower** on this page
or at the desk.

## Give a staff borrower app access

**Give app access** creates a sign-in so a staff member can see their own loans and holds in
[My Library](/docs/educonnect-library-my-library). Choose a username (3 to 64 characters: letters,
digits, dots, dashes, underscores and @, no spaces) and a first password. **Remove access** takes it
away. Teachers do not need this; they use the account they already have.

